.TH CHM-IMAGE-INSPECT 1
.SH NAME
chm-image-inspect \- inspect and transform images using OpenCV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chm-image-inspect
.I IMAGE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B chm-image-inspect --self-test
.br
.B chm-image-inspect --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decodes an image and reports dimensions, channel count, depth and mean channel values.
It can also write edge maps, grayscale images and resized images. Input files are read
as data; this tool does not execute embedded content.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print metadata as a JSON object.
.TP
.B --edges OUTPUT
Write a Canny edge map to OUTPUT.
.TP
.B --grayscale OUTPUT
Write a grayscale copy to OUTPUT.
.TP
.B --resize WIDTHxHEIGHT OUTPUT
Resize the input. Each dimension must be from 1 through 16384.
.TP
.B --self-test
Exercise OpenCV image encode/decode, grayscale conversion, Canny and resize operations.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 for an unreadable image; 3 for output-write failure; 64 for invalid arguments;
65 for unsupported channel layouts.
